<title>INDIA: India Cheminor Drugs 1996/97 net slips.</title>
<headline>India Cheminor Drugs 1996/97 net slips.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	   74.43     vs     184.95</p>
<p>    Net sales	 1,304.82     vs   1,263.74</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)     3.00     vs	 3.00</p>
<p>    Other income	 33.20     vs	18.50</p>
<p>    Expenditure     1,089.88     vs     975.00</p>
<p>    Interest	     93.39     vs	67.06</p>
<p>    Gross profit	154.75     vs     240.17</p>
<p>    Depreciation	 63.90     vs	55.22</p>
<p>    Tax		    16.41     vs	 nil</p>
<p>Note: Cheminor Drugs based in the southern city of Hyderabad said it had made a provision for tax in 1996/97 under a new minimum tax.</p>
<p>The firm said increase in interest costs and a fall in prices of most products in domestic markets affected net profits.</p>
<p>Exports fell to 863.94 million rupees from 907.81 million in 1995/96, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
